# Accessibility Standards

## ♿ **WCAG 2.2 AA Compliance**
- Ensure all UI components meet WCAG 2.2 AA standards
- Implement proper semantic HTML structure
- Provide meaningful alt text for images and descriptive labels for form elements
- Ensure keyboard navigation works for all interactive elements
- Maintain sufficient color contrast ratios (minimum 4.5:1 for normal text)
- Support screen readers with proper ARIA attributes
- Test with accessibility tools and assistive technologies
- Ensure focus indicators are visible and logical

## 🎨 **Frontend Accessibility Guidelines**
- **Semantic HTML**: Use proper HTML5 semantic elements (header, nav, main, section, article, aside, footer)
- **Form Labels**: Associate all form controls with descriptive labels
- **Alt Text**: Provide meaningful alternative text for all images
- **Color Contrast**: Ensure sufficient contrast ratios for text and background colors
- **Keyboard Navigation**: Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible
- **Focus Management**: Implement logical focus order and visible focus indicators
- **ARIA Attributes**: Use ARIA labels, roles, and properties appropriately
- **Screen Reader Support**: Test with screen readers and assistive technologies

## 🧪 **Accessibility Testing**
- Test with keyboard-only navigation
- Verify screen reader compatibility
- Check color contrast ratios
- Validate ARIA implementation
- Test with accessibility tools (axe, WAVE, etc.)
- Ensure focus indicators are visible
- Verify form labels and descriptions

## 📋 **Accessibility Checklist**
- ✅ **Semantic HTML structure** implemented
- ✅ **Form labels** properly associated
- ✅ **Alt text** provided for images
- ✅ **Color contrast** meets WCAG standards
- ✅ **Keyboard navigation** works for all elements
- ✅ **Focus indicators** are visible and logical
- ✅ **ARIA attributes** used appropriately
- ✅ **Screen reader testing** completed